# Wave W17-AD (Amber Sea — West): wake sand — warm gold-green shallows sand, wake-flecked: the first water out of Marisol, still gold with the shore and green with the shallows, carrying the ferry wake as short pale streaks combed west-east across the tread — the wake drawn as fleck register in the kind (design: coral heads in clear shallows, a ferry wake crossing the lane). West’s own sand — split from its twin Central by temperature and traffic entire (warm gold-green under the wake vs garden-bright still water) and from Maris’s bright sand (R219) by hue: this sand is olive-gold, that one pale lemon.
